      {
        "id": 88770,
        "name": "HeroComplex",
        "username": "HeroComplex",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/bbce88/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-05T12:53:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This actually does appear in one of the rulebooks!&nbsp; In my version of the Enhanced Edition rulebook, the reshuffle rule appears in Quick Reference quide on the inside cover/first page, in the final paragraph.&nbsp; \"If a card needs to be drawn or discarded from an empty deck, shuffle that deck's trash to recreate that deck and continue to play as normal.\"&nbsp; I see that this rule is missing from the EE rulebook that appears on the Downloads page, so I guess this is either only in some versions of the EE rulebook, or there is a mistake in the PDF, I really couldn't say which.&nbsp; But as far as wanting an official source to spell this out <span class=\"bbcode-i\">somewhere</span>, there you go.</p>",
